# Welcome Message Upgrade Plan

## Goal
Upgrade the Welcome Message feature to support **Text** and **Flex Message** types with a toggle UI, matching the reference design.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema ([prisma/schema.prisma](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/prisma/schema.prisma))
- Modify [WelcomeMessage](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/automation.actions.ts#10-21) model:
    - Ensure `messageType` is used (or map `type` request to it).
    - Add `altText` (String?) for Flex messages.
    - **Note**: EXISTING `content` (Json) will be preferred over a new `message` String field to maintain consistency with `AutoReplyKeyword` and allow structured data storage. The UI will handle stringifying/parsing.

    ```prisma
    model WelcomeMessage {
      // ... existing fields
      messageType MessageType @default(TEXT)
      content     Json
      altText     String? // [NEW] Use for Flex alt text
      // ...
    }
    ```

### 2. UI Updates ([src/components/automation/welcome-settings.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/automation/welcome-settings.tsx))
- Refactor the component to match the "Reference Image" layout:
    - **Header**: "Enable Welcome Message" switch.
    - **Message Type**: Big Radio Cards (Text vs Flex).
    - **Editor**:
        - **Text**: Simple Textarea.
        - **Flex**: JSON Editor (Textarea monospace) + "Alt Text" input + "Load Template" button (Simulated or actual if templates exist).

### 3. Server Actions (`src/actions/welcome.actions.ts`)
- Update [saveWelcomeMessage](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/automation.actions.ts#22-55) to accept `altText` and handle `messageType`.

### 4. Webhook Logic ([src/app/api/webhook/line/route.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/api/webhook/line/route.ts))
- Update [handleFollowEvent](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/api/webhook/line/route.ts#70-125):
    - Fetch [WelcomeMessage](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/automation.actions.ts#10-21).
    - Check `messageType`.
    - If `FLEX`: usage `lineClient.pushMessage` with `{ type: 'flex', altText: wm.altText, contents: wm.content }`.
    - If `TEXT`: usage `lineClient.pushMessage` with `{ type: 'text', text: wm.content.text }`.

## Verification
- Run migration.
- Test UI: Toggle types, save, reload.
- Test Webhook: Follow the bot, verify correct message type and content is received.
